IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er3-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 37 and 38: SUPPLEMENTAL UNEMPLOYMENT BENEFIT
-- PLANS, and MATERNITY LEAVE, LEAVE FOR THE CARE OF A CHILD AND COMPASSIONATE CARE LEAVE PLANS.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Reg 37 says when payments from an employer's plan are not earnings; reg 38 says how much of a top-up of
-- maternity, parental, family-care and similar leave pay is left out of earnings. Both are counting rules.
-- The judgment "the plan was submitted to the Commission" is a fact about the plan, an input.

§ `Regulation 37 -- supplemental unemployment benefit plans`

-- (2)(c) "requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments but may
-- provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for the reason that the employee (i)
-- is serving the waiting period, (ii) has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits,
-- or (iii) has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled".
-- The reasons for which a plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits are listed; a plan that pays
-- for any other reason does not meet (c).
-- src:674 | (c) requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments under the plan but may provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for the reason that the employee
-- src:675 | (i) is serving the waiting period,
-- src:676 | (ii) has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits, or
-- src:677 | (iii) has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(2)(c) (src:674-677)
DECLARE `er3 Reason a plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits` IS ONE OF
    `er3 reason: the employee is serving the waiting period`                                         -- (c)(i)
    `er3 reason: the employee has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits` -- (c)(ii)
    `er3 reason: the employee has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled`    -- (c)(iii)
    `er3 reason: some other reason`

GIVEN reason IS AN `er3 Reason a plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 37(2)(c) the reason is one of subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` IF
        reason EQUALS `er3 reason: the employee is serving the waiting period`
    OR reason EQUALS `er3 reason: the employee has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits`
    OR reason EQUALS `er3 reason: the employee has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled`

-- src:674 | (c) requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments under the plan but may provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for the reason that the employee
-- src:675 | (i) is serving the waiting period,
-- src:676 | (ii) has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits, or
-- src:677 | (iii) has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(2)(c) (src:674-677)
GIVEN `the plan requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons for which the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits` IS A LIST OF `er3 Reason a plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 37(2)(c) the plan requires application for and receipt of benefits, with only the permitted exceptions` IF
        `the plan requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments`
    AND all `reg 37(2)(c) the reason is one of subparagraphs (i) to (iii)` `the reasons for which the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits`

-- (2)(d) The plan must require that the combined weekly payments from the plan and the portion of the weekly
-- benefit rate from that employment not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that
-- employment. The most the plan may pay for a week follows from it.
-- src:678 | (d) requires that the combined weekly payments received from the plan and the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment do not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(2)(d) (src:678)
GIVEN `the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 37(2)(d) the most the plan may pay for a week` IS
    max 0 ((95% TIMES `the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment`) MINUS `the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment`)

-- (2)(g) The plan must require written notice of any change to the Commission within 30 days after the
-- effective date of the change. A notice on the 30th day after that date is in time (the keel's fork F4 in KEEL-NOTES.md,
-- not this piece's F4: the last day of the period counts).
-- src:681 | (g) requires that the plan be submitted to the Commission prior to its effective date and that written notice of any change to the plan be given to the Commission within 30 days after the effective date of the change;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(2)(g) (src:681)
GIVEN `the effective date of the change to the plan` IS A DATE
      `the day on which written notice of the change was given to the Commission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 37(2)(g) written notice of the change is given within 30 days after its effective date` IF
    `the day on which written notice of the change was given to the Commission` AT MOST (`the last day of` 30 `days after` `the effective date of the change to the plan`)

-- (2) A supplemental unemployment benefit plan is a plan with all nine features. Each input is a term of the
-- plan (what it "requires" or "provides"), stated by the person who has the plan.
-- src:671 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), a supplemental unemployment benefit plan is a plan that
-- src:672 | (a) identifies the group or groups of employees covered by the plan;
-- src:673 | (b) covers any period of unemployment by reason of a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury, quarantine or any combination of such reasons;
-- src:674 | (c) requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits in order to receive payments under the plan but may provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for the reason that the employee
-- src:675 | (i) is serving the waiting period,
-- src:676 | (ii) has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits, or
-- src:677 | (iii) has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled;
-- src:678 | (d) requires that the combined weekly payments received from the plan and the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment do not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment;
-- src:679 | (e) requires that payments under the plan be financed by the employer and that the employer keep separate accounts for those payments;
-- src:680 | (f) requires that, on termination of the plan, all remaining assets revert to the employer or be used for payments under the plan or for administrative costs of the plan;
-- src:681 | (g) requires that the plan be submitted to the Commission prior to its effective date and that written notice of any change to the plan be given to the Commission within 30 days after the effective date of the change;
-- src:682 | (h) provides that the employees have no vested right to payments under the plan, except to payments during a period of unemployment specified in the plan; and
-- src:683 | (i) provides that payments in respect of guaranteed annual remuneration or in respect of deferred remuneration or severance pay benefits are not reduced or increased by payments received under the plan.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(2) (src:671-683)
GIVEN `identifies the group or groups of employees covered by the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `covers any period of unemployment by reason of a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury, quarantine or any combination of such reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires application for and receipt of benefits, with only the permitted exceptions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires that the combined weekly payments from the plan and the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment do not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires that payments under the plan be financed by the employer and that the employer keep separate accounts for those payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires that, on termination of the plan, all remaining assets revert to the employer or be used for payments under the plan or for administrative costs of the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requires that the plan be submitted to the Commission prior to its effective date and that written notice of any change to the plan be given to the Commission within 30 days after the effective date of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provides that the employees have no vested right to payments under the plan, except to payments during a period of unemployment specified in the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provides that payments in respect of guaranteed annual remuneration or in respect of deferred remuneration or severance pay benefits are not reduced or increased by payments received under the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 37(2) supplemental unemployment benefit plan` IF
        `identifies the group or groups of employees covered by the plan`
    AND `covers any period of unemployment by reason of a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury, quarantine or any combination of such reasons`
    AND `requires application for and receipt of benefits, with only the permitted exceptions`
    AND `requires that the combined weekly payments from the plan and the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment do not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment`
    AND `requires that payments under the plan be financed by the employer and that the employer keep separate accounts for those payments`
    AND `requires that, on termination of the plan, all remaining assets revert to the employer or be used for payments under the plan or for administrative costs of the plan`
    AND `requires that the plan be submitted to the Commission prior to its effective date and that written notice of any change to the plan be given to the Commission within 30 days after the effective date of the change`
    AND `provides that the employees have no vested right to payments under the plan, except to payments during a period of unemployment specified in the plan`
    AND `provides that payments in respect of guaranteed annual remuneration or in respect of deferred remuneration or severance pay benefits are not reduced or increased by payments received under the plan`

-- (1) Payments received by a claimant as an insured person under such a plan are not earnings "for the purposes
-- of section 19, subsection 21(3), section 45 or 46, subsection 152.03(3) or section 152.18 of the Act": the
-- purpose of a deduction from benefits, or of ss 45 and 46. They are not mentioned for section 14 of the
-- Regulations (interruption of earnings), where reg 35 decides alone. "Subject to the other provisions of this
-- section": subsection (2) is the only other provision (subsection (3) is repealed).
-- src:670 | 37 (1) Subject to the other provisions of this section, payments received by a claimant as an insured person under a supplemental unemployment benefit plan are not earnings for the purposes of section 19, subsection 21(3), section 45 or 46, subsection 152.03(3) or section 152.18 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 37(1) (src:670)
GIVEN `the payments are received by a claimant as an insured person under a plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan is a supplemental unemployment benefit plan under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 37(1) payments under a supplemental unemployment benefit plan are not earnings for the purpose` IF
        `the payments are received by a claimant as an insured person under a plan`
    AND `the plan is a supplemental unemployment benefit plan under subsection (2)`
    AND (   purpose EQUALS `er3 purpose: the amount to be deducted from benefits`
         OR purpose EQUALS `er3 purpose: sections 45 and 46 of the Act`)

-- reg 37(3) [Repealed, SOR/2016-314, s. 1] (line 684).

§ `Regulation 38 -- maternity leave, leave for the care of a child and compassionate care leave plans`

-- (1) The payments are paid "because of pregnancy, for the care of a child or children referred to in
-- subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or for the care or support of a family member referred to in
-- subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or because
-- of any combination of those reasons". The reasons are the keel's `Reason for benefits`; illness, injury or
-- quarantine is not among them (it is dealt with in subsection (2)), nor is a regular benefit. A combination is
-- a non-empty list of reasons, every one of them listed.
-- src:687 | 38 (1) The following portion of any payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person because of pregnancy, for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or because of any combination of those reasons, is excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35, namely, the portion that
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 38(1) (src:687)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 38(1) the reason is one of those listed` IF
        reason EQUALS `pregnancy`
    OR reason EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a family member`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a critically ill child`
    OR reason EQUALS `care or support of a critically ill adult`

-- src:687 | 38 (1) The following portion of any payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person because of pregnancy, for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or because of any combination of those reasons, is excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35, namely, the portion that
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 38(1) (src:687)
GIVEN reasons IS A LIST OF `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 38(1) the payments are because of one or more of the reasons listed or any combination of them` IF
        NOT (null reasons)
    AND all `reg 38(1) the reason is one of those listed` reasons

-- (1)(a) and (b): the excluded portion is the part of the payments that, with the portion of the weekly benefit
-- rate from that employment, does not exceed the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment, and
-- that does not reduce accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or other accumulated
-- credits. The part that reduces credits is therefore never excluded.
-- src:687 | 38 (1) The following portion of any payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person because of pregnancy, for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or because of any combination of those reasons, is excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35, namely, the portion that
-- src:688 | (a) when combined with the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment, does not exceed that claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment; and
-- src:689 | (b) does not reduce the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits from that claimant's employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 38(1) (src:687-689)
GIVEN reasons IS A LIST OF `Reason for benefits`
      `the payments paid to the claimant as an insured person` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the payments that reduces the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 38(1) the portion of the payments excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35` IS
    IF `reg 38(1) the payments are because of one or more of the reasons listed or any combination of them` reasons
    THEN max 0 (min (`the payments paid to the claimant as an insured person` MINUS `the part of the payments that reduces the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits`)
                    (`the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` MINUS `the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment`))
    ELSE 0

-- reg 38(1.1) [Repealed, SOR/2016-314, s. 2] (line 690).

-- (2) However, the portion of the payments paid in respect of a week during which benefits are payable by reason
-- of illness, injury or quarantine is considered earnings for the purposes of section 35 (so nothing is excluded
-- for that week).
-- src:691 | (2) However, the portion of any payments referred to in subsection (1) that are paid to a claimant in respect of a week during which benefits are payable to them by reason of illness, injury or quarantine is considered earnings for the purposes of section 35.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 38(2) (src:691)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for the week by reason of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 38(2) the portion of the payments for the week is considered earnings` IF
    `benefits are payable to the claimant for the week by reason of illness, injury or quarantine`

-- src:687 | 38 (1) The following portion of any payments that are paid to a claimant as an insured person because of pregnancy, for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or because of any combination of those reasons, is excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35, namely, the portion that
-- src:688 | (a) when combined with the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment, does not exceed that claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment; and
-- src:689 | (b) does not reduce the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits from that claimant's employment.
-- src:690 | (1.1) [Repealed, SOR/2016-314, s. 2]
-- src:691 | (2) However, the portion of any payments referred to in subsection (1) that are paid to a claimant in respect of a week during which benefits are payable to them by reason of illness, injury or quarantine is considered earnings for the purposes of section 35.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 38(1), (2) (src:687-691)
GIVEN reasons IS A LIST OF `Reason for benefits`
      `the payments paid to the claimant as an insured person` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the payments that reduces the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `benefits are payable to the claimant for the week by reason of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 38 the portion of the payments for the week that is excluded as earnings` IS
    IF `reg 38(2) the portion of the payments for the week is considered earnings` `benefits are payable to the claimant for the week by reason of illness, injury or quarantine`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `reg 38(1) the portion of the payments excluded as earnings for the purposes of section 35` reasons `the payments paid to the claimant as an insured person` `the part of the payments that reduces the claimant's accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits` `the claimant's normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the portion of the claimant's weekly benefit rate from that employment`
